{"id":27625,"slug":"people-on-sunday","title":"People on Sunday","year":1930,"country":"Germany","duration":73,"spine":569,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27625-people-on-sunday","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/5f43a5464a0df8ce69cb8bf45774302d/B4zQse0843Uu8bVCONSjsowuOQ3D4n_large.jpg","description":"Years before they became major players in Hollywood, a group of young German filmmakers—including eventual noir masters Robert Siodmak and Edgar G. Ulmer and future Oscar winners Billy Wilder  and Fred Zinnemann—worked together on the once-in-a-lifetime collaboration People on Sunday (Menschen am Sonntag). This effervescent, sunlit silent, about a handful of city dwellers (a charming cast of nonprofessionals) enjoying a weekend outing, offers a rare glimpse of Weimar-era Berlin. A unique hybrid of documentary and fictional storytelling, People on Sunday was both an experiment and a mainstream hit that would influence generations of film artists around the world.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Robert Siodmak","slug":"robert-siodmak"},{"name":"Edgar G. Ulmer","slug":"edgar-g-ulmer"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Erwin Splettstösser","role":"Himself (taxi driver)","slug":"erwin-splettstosser"},{"actor":"Brigitte Borchert","role":"Herself (record seller)","slug":"brigitte-borchert"},{"actor":"Wolfgang von Waltershausen","role":"Himself (wine seller)","slug":"wolfgang-von-waltershausen"},{"actor":"Christl Ehlers","role":"Herself (extra in films)","slug":"christl-ehlers"},{"actor":"Annie Schreyer","role":"Herself (model)","slug":"annie-schreyer"},{"actor":"Kurt Gerron","role":"Himself","slug":"kurt-gerron"},{"actor":"Valeska Gert","role":"Herself","slug":"valeska-gert"},{"actor":"Heinrich Gretler","role":"Himself","slug":"heinrich-gretler"},{"actor":"Ernö Verebes","role":"Herself","slug":"erno-verebes"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Robert Siodmak","slug":"robert-siodmak"},{"role":"Director","person":"Edgar G. Ulmer","slug":"e